# Workflow files are checked here, not in CI: a workflow GitHub cannot parse
# never runs, so a job inside it can never report the problem. See
# scripts/workflow-lint.mjs.
node scripts/workflow-lint.mjs

# ⚠️ The three source-only gates run HERE as well as in CI, and the reason is
# measured: 1.075s for all six together. They need no build, no API and no
# browser, so there is no cost to catching their defects before the commit
# rather than after a push.
#
# The backtick trap is why. A backtick inside a component's inline template or
# styles literal terminates it, the build then fails with `TS1005: ',' expected`
# pointing at a line far from the cause, and it has now happened THIRTEEN times
# in this repository — five of them on 11 October alone, in the phases that
# wrote the lint. A note in CLAUDE.md did not stop it; a CI job catches it ten
# minutes later; this catches it at the moment it is written.
node scripts/template-literal-lint.mjs
node scripts/token-lint.mjs
node scripts/state-lint.mjs
node scripts/feedback-lint.mjs
node scripts/scale-lint.mjs
node scripts/font-lint.mjs
node scripts/control-contrast-audit.mjs

# ⚠️ Added v1.149.0, and it is a RATCHET, not a ban: 226 emoji were in the
# tree when the baseline was taken and they cannot all go in one change. The
# number may fall and never rise. It scans whole files rather than template
# literals, because the board went on rendering a house emoji twelve times
# after every emoji in the markup had been replaced — that one lived in a
# label map in the class, where a sweep of the markup cannot see it.
node scripts/emoji-lint.mjs

# 🔴 Added v1.150.0 after a commit shipped that did not compile. The icon set
# was expanded, migrated onto, driven and screenshotted — all green — and then
# `git checkout` on icon.ts, used to undo a falsification, discarded the whole
# expansion because the file still held uncommitted work. Every check that
# could have caught it had already run. A verification that happened before
# the last change is not a verification of what shipped; this one is source
# only and takes under a second.
node scripts/icon-lint.mjs

# 🔴 Added v1.153.0. A room card can carry seven badges over its photo, and
# they were declared across two files: .badge-new and .badge-verified both
# ended up solid sage on white — "listed a few days ago" and "this landlord's
# identity has been checked" rendering identically — and .badge-featured and
# .badge-sublet were both gold. Neither file was wrong on its own, which is
# why state-lint has guarded the same thing for .state--* since Phase 8.
# Compares resolved COLOUR, not the text of the declaration: the gold pair
